@flexiarg institutions/monitoring-users
@title Monitoring Users
@keywords monitoring, accountability, appropriation levels, Ostrom 4A, common-pool resources
@audience institution designers, commons researchers
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Ostrom design principle 4A, wording as in Cox, Arnold and Tomas (2010), "A review of design principles for community-based natural resource management", Ecology and Society 15(4):38, quoted in Corneli 2016 (ICCC 2016) Table 1. Original source Ostrom 1990, Governing the Commons. Drafted by claude-16 with Joe, 2026-10-29.
@status draft 2026-10-29; to vet against Ostrom 1990 and Cox et al. 2010 before relying on non-quoted text
@references [institutions/ARGUMENT creativity-commons/distributed-monitoring]

! conclusion:
  "Monitors who are accountable to the users monitor the appropriation and provision levels of the users."

  + context:
    Monitoring of what users take and contribute; the monitors may be users themselves.

  + IF:
    Rules limit what users take or require what they contribute.

  + HOWEVER:
    Monitors who answer to an outside body rather than the users can serve that body's interests instead.

  + THEN:
    Assign monitoring of appropriation and provision to people accountable to the users, and make their findings available to users.

  + BECAUSE:
    Rules nobody checks are not followed for long, and users trust monitoring they can hold to account.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Vet the HOWEVER and BECAUSE against Ostrom 1990 and Cox et al. 2010; only the conclusion is quoted.]
    next[Creativity-commons transposition: creativity-commons/distributed-monitoring.]
